WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.610
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:15.550
Last time: pixels → patterns → seeing!

3
00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:23.390
Chapter 2 · Can Computers Listen?

4
00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:31.310
No ears! So how can it hear?

5
00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:39.740
Meet Riya and her smart speaker

6
00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:49.300
"Hey helper, play my favourite song!"

7
00:00:49.300 --> 00:01:00.480
Aarav says "Play music"… nothing!

8
00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:11.090
How did it hear Riya? Why not Aarav?

9
00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:16.510
How a computer listens: 3 steps

10
00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:25.650
1 · It hears the sound of your voice

11
00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:41.980
2 · Sound → words: speech recognition

12
00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:51.870
3 · Words → patterns → what you want

13
00:01:51.870 --> 00:02:05.310
It learned from thousands of examples

14
00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:20.180
Many voices, many accents, more examples

15
00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:30.400
Not mind reading. Just patterns!

16
00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:36.390
A listening helper = a VOICE ASSISTANT

17
00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:43.270
Smart speakers: songs and weather

18
00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:49.240
Phone helpers: set alarms, call nani

19
00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:56.920
Voice typing: talk, and words appear

20
00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:03.910
Aarav forgot the WAKE WORD!

21
00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:14.450
Wake word = "Start listening now!"

22
00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:22.690
Like calling a friend's name first

23
00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:30.980
"Hey helper, play music!" It works!

24
00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:34.690
Some things make listening harder

25
00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:44.930
Noise: TV, mixer, busy market

26
00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:54.160
Whispers, mumbles, and talking too fast

27
00:03:54.160 --> 00:04:04.530
"Set a timer" → "Set a tiger?" Oops!

28
00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:21.410
The mixer is loud. What should Riya do?

29
00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:34.800
Wait for quiet, then ask clearly and fully

30
00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:52.390
Which voice command is good?

31
00:04:52.390 --> 00:05:07.880
Good = wake word + one short, clear ask

32
00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:17.780
Wake word · Speak clearly · Quiet room

33
00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:21.730
Your turn: practice check

34
00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:30.800
Write one clear command for a voice helper

35
00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:43.000
"Hey helper, what's the weather in Delhi?"

36
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:49.180
Listening = sound → words → patterns

37
00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:52.800
Say the wake word first

38
00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:55.210
Speak clearly in a quiet room

39
00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:59.840
Noise and whispers make it harder

40
00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:09.550
Chapter 2 done!

41
00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:16.350
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
